{"id": "EUVD-2026-103598", "enisaUuid": "b49605cf-fb35-3ff5-91cd-f180710c41a3", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nautofs: fix sbi->pipe file reference leak in autofs_kill_sb()\n\nWhen autofs_fill_super() fails before clearing AUTOFS_SBI_CATATONIC (for\nexample, when find_get_pid() fails on an invalid pgrp mount option, or\nwhen an fs_context is closed before mounting), deactivate_locked_super()\ninvokes autofs_kill_sb() -> autofs_catatonic_mode(sbi).\n\nBecause AUTOFS_SBI_CATATONIC is still set in sbi->flags,\nautofs_catatonic_mode() returns early without calling fput(sbi->pipe),\npermanently leaking the pipe struct file reference.\n\nExplicitly release sbi->pipe in autofs_kill_sb() if it is still non-NULL\nafter autofs_catatonic_mode().", "datePublished": "2026-10-18T15:18:20", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-19T09:21:36", "baseScore": 0.0, "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/3684e2273ba94553af3c5195a46a50214a1a96e3", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/0662b1ff9b383d5a233d344e4dc518c27a17f7b8", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/34fa4c1c6e10507dc60e35a82cc9655666946cfd", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/a58593b501b7be5ad2bc5181bfa8cd4599be257c", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/f1c57f5b16bbc3571bd479c290996c4d4e1fb931", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/4bcb371019097d0e357f097902587401c509bbc9", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/fc4fd0281ac80b5a3c5a2330f688f0f9d2a420b6", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/aa5e44b29ffe4eaa08cc2237fd65bc2596bc023e"], "aliases": ["GHSA-j44w-wp8g-33m4", "CVE-2026-98553"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.21, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0579802f-a437-3e39-80a5-e8ada7e2071e", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.9"}, {"id": "149d6f00-39cb-3979-b354-ad095aba46ea", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "ebc921ca9b92a3cf304d99bd7b7f373ec78c7ed7 <4bcb371019097d0e357f097902587401c509bbc9"}, {"id": "18aa83b